@startuml divergence-flow
' How a per-axis change becomes (or fails to become) an observed fork.
' Colour key: play = blue · replay = green · disagreement = red · benign = grey

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBorderThickness 1.5
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #F57F17
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F

title <b>From an axis change to a fork — the propagation a reviewer must trace</b>\n<size:11>Every register entry states where on this path its change lands, and where it stops.</size>

start
:**A node upgrades.**\nOne of the six axes moves for some class of program;
note right #E3F2FD
  <b>Mixed-version network is the premise.</b>
  <i>Validate::version</i> (<i>casper/src/rust/validate.rs:273</i>)
  compares block versions for <b>EXACT equality</b> against a
  genesis-anchored constant. There is <b>no activation height</b>
  and no per-feature gate, so a consensus change ships as a
  <b>coordinated version bump</b>, which is a network act.
end note

if (Does any deployed program\nreach the changed code?) then (no)
  :**LATENT.**\nMechanism proven, no witness.\nRecord as //potential//, do not upgrade\nto "does break".;<<#ECEFF1>>
  stop
else (yes)
endif

partition "PLAY — the proposer" #E3F2FD {
  :Normalize the deploy source\n<size:10>Axis 5 can refuse here</size>;
  :Reduce; count committed COMMs\n<size:10>Axes 1, 2, 6</size>;
  :Serialise events and state\n<size:10>Axis 3 — bincode lane</size>;
  :Commit the post-state root\n<size:10>Axis 4</size>;
  :Encode the block\n<size:10>Axis 3 — prost lane</size>;
}

partition "REPLAY — every other validator" #E8F5E9 {
  :Decode the block;
  :Re-execute the deploy against\nthe recorded COMM trace;
  :Recompute events, state root,\nand //error_message//;
}

if (Do play and replay agree?) then (yes)
  :**Block accepted.**;<<#C8E6C9>>
  stop
else (no)
  if (Which comparison failed?) then (post-state root)
    :**SAFETY FORK.**\nHonest nodes hold\ndifferent chains.;<<#FFCDD2>>
  elseif (//is_failed// / //error_message//) then ( )
    :**SLASHABLE FAULT.**\n<size:11>ReplayFailure ⇒ InvalidBlock::InvalidTransaction</size>\n<size:10>//is_slashable() == true// (block_status.rs:203)</size>\n<size:10>Deterministic across validators, so this is</size>\n<size:10>liveness + slashing — not a silent safety fork.</size>;<<#F8BBD0>>
  else (the process died)
    :**LIVENESS SPLIT.**\nA stack overflow is a SIGSEGV,\nnot an //Err//: uncatchable,\nunreachable by metering.;<<#FFF9C4>>
  endif
  stop
endif
@enduml
